<p>From a <a href="https://archive.org/details/journalofsociety17soci/page/98/mode/2up">1915 examination</a> of Darkie, a blind New Zealand terrier who barked answers to his master&#8217;s queries:</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-21-science-marches-on-1.jpg" alt="https://archive.org/details/journalofsociety17soci/page/100/mode/2up" width="593" height="464" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-73789" srcset="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-21-science-marches-on-1.jpg 593w, https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-21-science-marches-on-1-300x235.jpg 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 593px) 100vw, 593px" /></p>
<p>From the local <em>Lyttelton Times</em>, June 12:</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-21-science-marches-on-2.jpg" alt="https://archive.org/details/journalofsociety17soci/page/104/mode/2up" width="592" height="404" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-73782" srcset="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-21-science-marches-on-2.jpg 592w, https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-21-science-marches-on-2-300x205.jpg 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 592px) 100vw, 592px" /></p>
<p>Apparently the dog was also clairvoyant:</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-21-science-marches-on-3-1.jpg" alt="https://archive.org/details/journalofsociety17soci/page/104/mode/2up" width="595" height="239" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-73795" srcset="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-21-science-marches-on-3-1.jpg 595w, https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-21-science-marches-on-3-1-300x121.jpg 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 595px) 100vw, 595px" /></p>
<p>Further questions successfully answered: &#8220;How many roods in one acre? How many furlongs in one mile? How many ounces in one pound avoirdupois? How many troy ounces? How many lbs. in one stone? What is the day of the month? What is the month of the year? What is the year over 1900?&#8221;</p>
<p>The Society for Psychical Research raised the prospect that the dog was merely continuing to respond until it received a cue to stop, as other performing animals had been discovered to do. It asked its New Zealand correspondent to test this hypothesis, but as far as I can tell he never did.</p>
